2. Implementing Brute Force in JavaScript: To implement a brute force attack in JavaScript, you'll need a function that generates all possible combinations and another function to check each combination against the target. Here's a simple example for a 4-digit PIN:

```javascript
function generateCombinations(length) {
    let combinations = [];
    for (let i = 1000; i <= 9999; i++) {
        combinations.push(i);
    }
    return combinations;
}

function checkPin(pin, target) {
